eywords** Multidimensional continued fractions · Polyhedral surfaces · Integer geometry\n\n## 1 Notation and Definitions\n\n### 1.1 Tensegrities\n\nThe subject of tensegrities was first considered by J.C. Maxwell in Maxwell (1864), who started to investigate first questions regarding force-loads for frameworks. Nowadays tensegrities are one of the leading directions of study in modern theory of rigidity (see, e.g., Connelly (1993) for further information). Let us recall several standard definitions.\n\n¹ Department of Mathematical Sciences, University of Liverpool, Mathematical Sciences Building, Liverpool L69 7ZL, UK\n\nOleg Karpenkov  \nkarpenk@liverpool.ac.uk--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpen problems on configuration spaces of tensegrities - MaRDI portal (https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/wiki/Open_problems_on_configuration_spaces_of_tensegrities)\nciteturn1338search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.0 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Open problems on configuration spaces of tensegrities ... Authors Oleg Karpenkov ... This page was built for publication: Open problems on configuration spaces of tensegrities\n# Open problems on configuration spaces of tensegrities\n\nFrom MaRDI portal\n\nJump to:navigation, search\n\nDOI10.1007/S40598-018-0080-7MaRDI QIDQ1617456zbMATH OpenOpenAlexFDO\n\nAuthors Oleg Karpenkov\n\nPublication date 8 November 2018\n\nPublished in Arnold Mathematical Journal (Search for Journal in Brave)\n\nCopyright license Image Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International\n\nFull work available at URL https://doi.org/10.1007/s40598-018-0080-7\n\nzbMATH Keywords\n\ninteger geometrymultidimensional continued fractionspolyhedral surfaces\n\nMathematics Subject Classification ID\n\nGraph representations (geometric and intersection representations, etc.) (05C62) Rigidity and flexibility of structures (aspects of discrete geometry) (52C25)\n\nThis page was built for publication: Open problems on configur